rvices and  give us stronger workers rights our  nation of grafters have earned a fair  day's pay for a fair day's work that  means a 15 pound minimum wage as soon as  possible Fair pay agreements to get  wages Rising for everyone and it's time  to do right by the people who've done us  all proud they got us through the  pandemic and we owe them give public  servants a proper pay rise a real pay  rise and give it now  and on November the 2nd from every  corner of the UK we will rally to  Westminster and if the share of a  government is still clinging to Power by  then we will demand that general  election  we are trade unionists just as when the  TUC proposed the furlough scheme at the  start of the pandemic we've got answers  to the problems that Britain faces we've  seen the difference our movement makes  right around the world and from Amazon  to Starbucks growing membership winning  deals proof that solidarity Works backed  up by new laws from Progressive  governments from Spain to New Zealand  and we hope soon Brazil too governments  who know that good jobs and Rising wages  are the route to a decent life  change can come and we can build it  remember those kids remember those kids  who save half their school dinners to  take home for tea remember pension is  too poor to keep warm and workers who  can't afford to get sick while NHS  waiting time saw none of this is  inevitable these are political choices  made by politicians and we can vote them  out  now as unions our job is to win now and  every day the bigger our movement the  stronger we are so informally moving the  general council's statement let's reach  out and tell workers why they should  join unions  you see trade unionism is the reasonable  notion that your boss doesn't have all  the answers that working people together  have a voice and have power and how that  changes everything we are the people who  brought you the weekend the eight hour  day equal pay we're proud of our  diversity our wonderful president Sue  ferns Dr Roach the brilliant who's  brilliantly LED our campaign Against  Racism we stand up for our class  we stand up for our class and it's a  multi-ethnic multi-racial working class  of men and women in cities towns and the  countryside too we're for all working  people yes we've got members on the  railways and shops and factories but  also in Uber deliveroo and Amazon  whatever our background racial religion  everyone deserves a decent job a pension  respect it wasn't wages or workers that  caused this crisis and we refuse to let  workers pay for it people ask me will  the TUC coordinate strike action this  winter and I say we already are  when workers are left with no choice but  to vote for strike action for decent pay  I say bring it on for the last 10 years  I've been proud to lead the TUC and I'm  passing the torch to my comrade the  brilliant poll Novak  at heart I've always believed always  always believed that trade unionism is  about friendship friendship between  workers transforms what is possible  Congress we have hope hoping young  workers joining unions workers backing  workers black workers and white workers  standing together let's take that  message to workplaces and communities in  every corner of the country we can build  a better world we will fight for our  class and together we all win solidarity  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  well follow that thank you very much  Francis it's not a time for goodbyes yet  but I do want to say a huge and a  heartfelt thank you from everyone for  all that you've done for the movement in  your time as general secretary  and let's all remember that your  leadership has guided us through  incredibly challenging times austerity  back again brexit pandemic cost of  living crisis and it has been invaluable  so thank you for everything that you've  done genuinely  right Congress we now have to move back  to the four

